# SSHFP (SSH Fingerprint) Records
# ====================================
# SSHFP records store SSH public key fingerprints in DNS for verification,
# allowing SSH clients to verify server keys against DNS before first connection.
#
# Format: SSHFP <algorithm> <fingerprint-type> <fingerprint>
#   - Algorithm: 1 = RSA, 2 = DSA, 3 = ECDSA, 4 = Ed25519
#   - Fingerprint Type: 1 = SHA-1, 2 = SHA-256
#   - Fingerprint: Hex-encoded hash of the public key
#
# For Trigger service SSH keys:
#   - Ed25519 key (SHA-256): <fingerprint-here>
#   - RSA key (SHA-256): <fingerprint-here>
#
# Generate SSHFP from known_hosts:
#   ssh-keygen -r hostname -f /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub | awk '{print $3, $2, $1}'
#   ssh-keygen -r hostname -f /etc/ssh/ssh_host_rsa_key.pub | awk '{print $3, $2, $1}'
#
# NOTE: Authoritative SSHFP records are defined in security/bind9/trigger.zone
# This file is provided for web servers that serve .well-known/ for documentation.
#
# For more information: RFC 4255 (SSHFP)
# https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4255
#
# Current status: SSHFP records are commented out in DNS zone file
# (require actual key fingerprints from deployment servers)
# Uncomment and populate in security/bind9/trigger.zone when keys are generated.
